<p id="S1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-th" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-th</annotation></semantics></math> eigenvalue of the fractional Laplacian, that is,</p>
