</table>
<p id="S1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;s&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;s&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\Delta)^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\Delta)^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="S1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(-\Delta)^{s}u(x):=C_{n,s}\lim_{\delta\rightarrow 0^{+}}\int_{\{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}:|y-x|\geq\delta\}}\frac{u(x)-u(y)}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dy." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></munder><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\Delta)^{s}u(x):=C_{n,s}\lim_{\delta\rightarrow 0^{+}}\int_{\{y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}:|y-x|\geq\delta\}}\frac{u(x)-u(y)}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dy.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The interest in our free boundary problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) arises from a natural generalization of the problem of minimizing <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-th" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-th</annotation></semantics></math> eigenvalue of <math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. However, even in this case, the problem is imperfectly understood. We refer the reader to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> for a detailed discussion. A classic breakthrough was given in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, which shows that such problems admit minimizers in the class of quasi-open sets, and is further improved in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>. The boundary regularity is recently developed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>, and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We note that (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) can be considered as a vector-valued version of the classical Bernoulli type free boundary problem. The scalar version of the one-phase Bernoulli type problem is studied in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> and a more generalized two-phase version is studied in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The fractional Laplacian has attracted many interests in the last years. Besides being a natural generalization of the Laplacian, such non-local operators often arise in different fields, including probability theory, mathematical physics, and applied sciences. For a comprehensive discussion of this type of non-local operator, we refer the reader to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>. Therefore, it is natural to study the free boundary problem in the setting of the fractional Laplacian. Such Bernoulli-type free boundary problems involving <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\Delta)^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\Delta)^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> are studied in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, for the one-phase problem, and the two-phase problem is studied in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. One main estimate that we use is developed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We point out that there are three main difficulties in studying problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>). Firstly, the eigenvalues are given by a min-max of the Rayleigh quotient which is a critical point of the functional instead of the minimum in, for example, the Bernoulli problem. We overcome this difficulty by following the idea of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>. A major problem arises when the multiplicity of the minimizing eigenvalue is not <math id="S1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, in which case, eigenfunctions might be degenerate.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Second, <math id="S1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\Delta)^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\Delta)^{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-local, which poses more technical difficulties than the local case, where we used estimates and techniques in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>. The non-locality also gives rise to the difficulty in studying the global configuration of minimizers due to the interaction between different pieces of the domain. To capture the behavior at infinity, our strategy is to study minimizers on a union of different copies of <math id="S1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> that don’t interact with each other (Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm3" title="Definition 2.3. ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Third, it is not a priori clear over what class of sets that we are minimizing over. To deal with this, we rephrase the problem using level sets of <math id="S1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{s,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{s,2}</annotation></semantics></math> functions. We note it is not necessary to do so and one could follow the idea of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> and consider the minimization problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) in the class of appropriate quasi-open sets. The main benefit of our approach is that we avoid the potential theory involved completely, and we refer the reader to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> for discussions on capacity and quasi-open sets.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Main Results.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.4</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists an open bounded measurable set <math id="S1.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A\subset\cup_{i=1}^{k}{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0em">⊂</mo><mo lspace="0em">∪</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subset\cup_{i=1}^{k}{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the minimum of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) is achieved, that is</span></p>
<table id="S1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(A)+|A|\leq\inf\{\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime})+|A^{\prime}|\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(A)+|A|\leq\inf\{\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime})+|A^{\prime}|\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Here the infimum is taken over a set of appropriate domains in <math id="S1.p9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\cup_{i=1}^{k}{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∪</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cup_{i=1}^{k}{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which will be made precise in the next section. We point out that in the local case, minimizers are given by unions of disjoint sets <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, which are translation invariant. In the nonlocal case, it could happen that these disjoint pieces are infinitely away from each other, and thus we consider the existence of minimizers in copies of <math id="S1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.6</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists an eigenfunction <math id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to the minimizing eigenvalue <math id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>), such that <math id="S1.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}\in C^{0,s}(\overline{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}\in C^{0,s}(\overline{A})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to the local case discussed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>, the perturbation of eigenfunctions gives information about a linear combination of the eigenfunctions corresponding to <math id="S1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore, Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm6" title="Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.6</span></a> only guarantee Hölder continuity for one eigenfunction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> is simple, we moreover have the following results.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.7</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the minimizing eigenvalue <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) is simple. Let <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the corresponding eigenfunction to <math id="S1.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Non-degeneracy.) For all </span><math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, there exists </span><math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, such that for </span><math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|B_{r/8}(x_{0})\cap A|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|B_{r/8}(x_{0})\cap A|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, we have</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{B_{r}(x_{0})}|u_{k}|\geq c_{0}r^{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{B_{r}(x_{0})}|u_{k}|\geq c_{0}r^{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Separation of the free boundary.)</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial\{u_{k}(x)&gt;0\}\cap\partial\{u_{k}(x)&lt;0\}=\varnothing." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">∩</mo><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\{u_{k}(x)&gt;0\}\cap\partial\{u_{k}(x)&lt;0\}=\varnothing.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Density estimate.) Suppose </span><math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a free boundary point, then there exists </span><math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C,r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C,r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for all </span><math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> small, we have</span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle|\{u_{k}&gt;0\}\cap B_{r}(x)|\geq Cr^{n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\{u_{k}&gt;0\}\cap B_{r}(x)|\geq Cr^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle|\{u_{k}=0\}\cap B_{r}(x)|\geq Cr^{n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\{u_{k}=0\}\cap B_{r}(x)|\geq Cr^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and </span><math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\partial A|=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\partial A|=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Free boundary regularity.) Let </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the extension of </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (defined in section </span><a href="#S5" title="5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">). Assume that </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u\|_{C^{0,s}(B_{1})}\leq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u\|_{C^{0,s}(B_{1})}\leq C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|u-U|\leq\tau_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|u-U|\leq\tau_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> where </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (depending only on </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n},y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n},y</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">), in polar coordinates </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}=\rho\cos(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}=\rho\cos(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\rho\sin(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\rho\sin(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, is</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U(x,y)=\rho^{1/2}\cos(\theta/2)^{2s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>cos</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(x,y)=\rho^{1/2}\cos(\theta/2)^{2s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F(u)=\partial\{u_{k}\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(u)=\partial\{u_{k}\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1,\gamma_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1,\gamma_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, for some constant </span><math id="S1.I1.i4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I1.i4.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Outline of paper.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">In section <a href="#S2" title="2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we give a formal definition of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>). In particular, we extend our domain to a union of <math id="S1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> copies of <math id="S1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. We introduce notation, and prove some useful preliminary estimates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Sections <a href="#S3" title="3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#S4" title="4. Existence of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> deal with the existence of minimizers. We first prove an a priori estimate showing that shape minimizers have to be bounded following the idea of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>. Using the boundedness of minimizers we show the existence of shape minimizers of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S5" title="5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we prove optimal regularity for some eigenfunctions. However, it is not clear which eigenfunction has such regularity due to the difficulty mentioned earlier, and we assume that <math id="S1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is simple in the rest of the paper. In Section <a href="#S6" title="6. Non-degeneracy ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we prove that the corerrsponding eigenfunction is non-degenerate.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S7" title="7. Blow-up Analysis ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we follow the idea of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> and conduct blow-up analysis using a Weiss type monotonicity formula and we conclude that the free boundaries are separated in Section <a href="#S8" title="8. Separation of the Free Boundary and Density Estimates ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. This behavior of separation also yields density estimates. In Section <a href="#S9" title="9. Free Boundary Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, we show that the eigenfunction corresponding to the minimizing <math id="S1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is an almost minimizer in the setting of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, which implies that the free boundary is <math id="S1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1,\gamma_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1,\gamma_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p17.1" class="ltx_p">In the Section <a href="#S10" title="10. The Global Configuration and a Toy Problem ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, we study the stability of the shape minimizer under translations and pose a toy problem that helps us in understanding the global configuration. In particular, we conjecture that there is no stable configurations where the disconnected pieces can interact with each other, and the minimizer has to be a union of <math id="S1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> congruent balls in different copies of <math id="S1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, this implies that <math id="S1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is not simple.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2. </span>Preliminaries</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce notations, definitions, and preliminary results in this section.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be any measurable set. Define the Sobolev space <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}^{s,2}_{0}(\Omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}^{s,2}_{0}(\Omega)</annotation></semantics></math> as the completion of <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}^{\infty}(\Omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}^{\infty}(\Omega)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the Gagliardo norm</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[u]_{W^{s,2}}:=\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{|u(x)-u(y)|^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[u]_{W^{s,2}}:=\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{|u(x)-u(y)|^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We always understand the problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) in the following sense.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.3</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}=\cup_{i=1}^{k}{\mathbb{R}}_{i}^{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">∪</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}=\cup_{i=1}^{k}{\mathbb{R}}_{i}^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is identical to <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> indexed by <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. We say <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{i}=u|_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i}}\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}({\mathbb{R}}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{i}=u|_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i}}\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}({\mathbb{R}}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the following class of functions</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathfrak{S}_{k}=\{u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}):|{\{u\neq 0\}}|&lt;C\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&lt;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{S}_{k}=\{u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}):|{\{u\neq 0\}}|&lt;C\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Define the Rayleigh quotient</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}_{k}=\frac{1}{\int_{\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}}|u|^{2}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{k}\frac{(u^{i}(x)-u^{j}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℜ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}_{k}=\frac{1}{\int_{\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}}|u|^{2}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{k}\frac{(u^{i}(x)-u^{j}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We understand problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) in the following sense.</p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda_{k}+|\{u\neq 0\}|=\min_{V_{k}\subset\mathfrak{S}_{k}}\max_{u\in V_{k}}\frac{1}{\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}|u|^{2}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{(u^{i}(x)-u^{i}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy+|\{u\neq 0\}|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}+|\{u\neq 0\}|=\min_{V_{k}\subset\mathfrak{S}_{k}}\max_{u\in V_{k}}\frac{1}{\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}|u|^{2}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{(u^{i}(x)-u^{i}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy+|\{u\neq 0\}|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where the minimum is taken over <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> dimensional subspace <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{S}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{S}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In Definition 2.3. ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>), we say</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A=\{u\neq 0\}=\{u^{1}\neq 0\}\cup\cdots\cup\{u^{k}\neq 0\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\{u\neq 0\}=\{u^{1}\neq 0\}\cup\cdots\cup\{u^{k}\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">a <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-minimizer</span>, call <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> the <span id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">minimizing eigenvalue</span> and <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> the <span id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">corresponding eigenfunction</span>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2.6</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The motivation for above definition is due to a concentration compactness phenomenon. Unlike in the local case where one can translate the domain, it could happen that a minimizing sequence of domains has disjoint pieces that move away from each other. We consider the limiting “infinitely away pieces” as lying in different copies of <math id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and don’t interact with each other. When <math id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}={\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}={\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the above definition of <math id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℜ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the usual Rayleigh quotient. 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2.7</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It is intentional that our space <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{S}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{S}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and the eigenvalue that we are interested in minimizing <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> depend on the same <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, since for minimizing <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need at most <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> copies of <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, for any <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}&gt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}&gt;k</annotation></semantics></math>, any k dimensional subspace of <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{S}_{k^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{S}_{k^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{S}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{S}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In Definition 2.3. ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>) is equivalent to</p>
<table id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{V_{k}\subset\mathfrak{S}_{k^{\prime}}}\max_{u\in V_{k}}\frac{1}{\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k^{\prime}}}|u|^{2}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{k^{\prime}}\frac{(u^{i}(x)-u^{i}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy+\{u\neq 0\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></munder><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{V_{k}\subset\mathfrak{S}_{k^{\prime}}}\max_{u\in V_{k}}\frac{1}{\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k^{\prime}}}|u|^{2}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{k^{\prime}}\frac{(u^{i}(x)-u^{i}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy+\{u\neq 0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It could happen that we only need <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math> copies, and in this case we have <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u|_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{j}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u|_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{j}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_notns">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notations 2.8</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i},y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i},y\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, we formally define</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x-y|=+\infty\quad\text{ and }\quad\frac{1}{|x-y|}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x-y|=+\infty\quad\text{ and }\quad\frac{1}{|x-y|}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In particular, for <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{k}\frac{(u^{i}(x)-u^{j}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy=\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{k}\frac{(u^{i}(x)-u^{j}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy=\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R[u]:=\mathfrak{R}_{k}[u]=\frac{1}{\int_{\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}}|u|^{2}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℜ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R[u]:=\mathfrak{R}_{k}[u]=\frac{1}{\int_{\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}}|u|^{2}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For any measurable <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subset\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subset\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{S}_{k}(A)=\{u\in\mathfrak{S}_{k}:u=0\text{ a.e. on }\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\setminus A\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> a.e. on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{S}_{k}(A)=\{u\in\mathfrak{S}_{k}:u=0\text{ a.e. on }\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\setminus A\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> be the kernel:</p>
<table id="S2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(x,y)=\frac{1}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(x,y)=\frac{1}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B[\cdot,\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B[\cdot,\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> be the inner product of <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B[u,v]=\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))(v(x)-v(y))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B[u,v]=\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))(v(x)-v(y))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.7" class="ltx_p">We sometimes omit the domain of integration if the domain the whole space, and we omit <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dxdy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dxdy</annotation></semantics></math> when there is no confusion.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.11</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any measurable <math id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\in\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\in\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say <math id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is a weak solution to</p>
<table id="S2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}(-\Delta)^{s}u=f\ &amp;\hbox{in}~\Omega,\\
u=0&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\setminus\Omega,\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}(-\Delta)^{s}u=f\ &amp;\hbox{in}~\Omega,\\
u=0&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\setminus\Omega,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.2" class="ltx_p">if <math id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathfrak{S}_{k}(\Omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathfrak{S}_{k}(\Omega)</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="S2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}(\varphi(x)-\varphi(y))dxdy=\int_{\Omega}u\varphi dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}(\varphi(x)-\varphi(y))dxdy=\int_{\Omega}u\varphi dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.3" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi\in C^{\infty}_{c}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi\in C^{\infty}_{c}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, that is <math id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi|_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i}}\in C^{\infty}_{c}({\mathbb{R}}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi|_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i}}\in C^{\infty}_{c}({\mathbb{R}}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We proceed to prove some useful estimates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2.12</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies in the weak sense:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}(-\Delta)^{s}u=\lambda u\ &amp;\hbox{in}~\{u\neq 0\},\\
u=0&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\setminus\{u\neq 0\},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">in</mtext><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}(-\Delta)^{s}u=\lambda u\ &amp;\hbox{in}~\{u\neq 0\},\\
u=0&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\setminus\{u\neq 0\},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in L^{\infty}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in L^{\infty}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u\|_{L^{\infty}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}\leq C\lambda^{\frac{n}{2s}}\|u\|_{L^{2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u\|_{L^{\infty}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}\leq C\lambda^{\frac{n}{2s}}\|u\|_{L^{2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Omega=\{u\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega=\{u\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(t,x)=e^{-\lambda t}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(t,x)=e^{-\lambda t}u</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\times[0,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\times[0,T)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in L^{2}(\tilde{W}^{s,2}_{0}(\Omega))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in L^{2}(\tilde{W}^{s,2}_{0}(\Omega))</annotation></semantics></math> is a weak solution to the heat equation:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}\partial_{t}v+(-\Delta)^{s}v=0&amp;\hbox{in}~\Omega\times[0,\infty),\\
v(0,x)=u(x)&amp;\hbox{in}~\Omega\times\{t=0\}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}\partial_{t}v+(-\Delta)^{s}v=0&amp;\hbox{in}~\Omega\times[0,\infty),\\
v(0,x)=u(x)&amp;\hbox{in}~\Omega\times\{t=0\}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">For every <math id="S2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we extend <math id="S2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(t,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(t,x)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and still denote it <math id="S2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have in the weak sense:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}|v|+(-\Delta)^{s}|v|\leq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}|v|+(-\Delta)^{s}|v|\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">We want to compare <math id="S2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> with another function <math id="S2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> defined in the following ways. First extend <math id="S2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and denote the extended function by <math id="S2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> be the solution to the following heat equation:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}\partial_{t}w+(-\Delta)^{s}w=0&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times[0,\infty),\\
w(0,x)=\tilde{u}(x)&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times\{t=0\}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}\partial_{t}w+(-\Delta)^{s}w=0&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times[0,\infty),\\
w(0,x)=\tilde{u}(x)&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times\{t=0\}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">We claim that:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|v|\leq w." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|v|\leq w.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, <math id="S2.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|v|-w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|v|-w</annotation></semantics></math> is a subsolution and</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\partial\Omega\times[0,T)}|v|-w=\max_{\partial\Omega\times[0,T)}-w\leq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\partial\Omega\times[0,T)}|v|-w=\max_{\partial\Omega\times[0,T)}-w\leq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality used the maximum principle for <math id="S2.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>. Using maximum principle again, we conclude that <math id="S2.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|v|\leq w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|v|\leq w</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">We also know:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(t,x)=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}p(x-y,t)u(y)dy," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(t,x)=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}p(x-y,t)u(y)dy,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S2.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the fractional heat kernel. It is known, for example from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p(x,t)|\leq C\min\{t^{-\frac{n}{2s}},\frac{t}{|x|^{n+2s}}\}\leq Ct^{-\frac{n}{2s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p(x,t)|\leq C\min\{t^{-\frac{n}{2s}},\frac{t}{|x|^{n+2s}}\}\leq Ct^{-\frac{n}{2s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|v(t,x)|\leq w(t,x)\leq\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}|p(x-y,t)||u(y)|dy\leq Ct^{-\frac{n}{2s}}\|u\|_{L^{1}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}\leq Ct^{-\frac{n}{2s}}\|u\|_{L^{2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|v(t,x)|\leq w(t,x)\leq\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}|p(x-y,t)||u(y)|dy\leq Ct^{-\frac{n}{2s}}\|u\|_{L^{1}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}\leq Ct^{-\frac{n}{2s}}\|u\|_{L^{2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.9.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we observe that:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|u(x)|=|e^{\lambda t}v(t,x)|\leq Ce^{\lambda t}t^{-\frac{n}{2s}}\|u\|_{L^{2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}\leq C\lambda^{\frac{n}{2s}}\|u\|_{L^{2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|u(x)|=|e^{\lambda t}v(t,x)|\leq Ce^{\lambda t}t^{-\frac{n}{2s}}\|u\|_{L^{2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}\leq C\lambda^{\frac{n}{2s}}\|u\|_{L^{2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.10.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows from choosing <math id="S2.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\frac{n}{2s\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\frac{n}{2s\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.15</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Cacciopoli inequality.) Let <math id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in{\mathfrak{S}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in{\mathfrak{S}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the weak solution of</span></p>
<table id="S2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(-\Delta)^{s}u=f\text{ in }\{u\neq 0\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> in </mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\Delta)^{s}u=f\text{ in }\{u\neq 0\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L^{1}(U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L^{1}(U)</annotation></semantics></math>, for some <math id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subset\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subset\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> open, containing <math id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{u\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any <math id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{r}\subset\{u\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}\subset\{u\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2.17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{B_{9r/10}}\int_{B_{9r/10}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}\leq\sup_{B_{r}}u\|f\|_{L^{1}(B_{r})}+Cr^{n}\|u\|_{L^{\infty}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}\sup_{B_{r}}|u|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></munder><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{B_{9r/10}}\int_{B_{9r/10}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}\leq\sup_{B_{r}}u\|f\|_{L^{1}(B_{r})}+Cr^{n}\|u\|_{L^{\infty}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}\sup_{B_{r}}|u|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth cutoff such that <math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=1</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{9r/10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{9r/10}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0</annotation></semantics></math> outside <math id="S2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\nabla\eta|\leq Cr^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\nabla\eta|\leq Cr^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Multiply (<a href="#S2.E16" title="In Lemma 2.15. ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.16</span></a>) by <math id="S2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{2}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{2}u</annotation></semantics></math> and integration by part gives</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))(\eta(x)u(x)-\eta(y)u(y))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}f\eta^{2}u\leq\sup_{B_{r}}u\|f\|_{L^{1}(B_{r})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></munder><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))(\eta(x)u(x)-\eta(y)u(y))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}f\eta^{2}u\leq\sup_{B_{r}}u\|f\|_{L^{1}(B_{r})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">We note that for the left hand side,</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
