<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3. </span>Boundedness of Shape Minimizers</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we make use of the observation of Bucur in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> that our shape minimizer, <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A=\{u\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\{u\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math> in problem (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In Definition 2.3. ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>) is a priori a local shape subsolution. Then we prove that if <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is a local shape subsolution, then it must be bounded.
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define the torsion energy:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(A):=\min_{u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}\frac{1}{2}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy-\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}u(x)dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(A):=\min_{u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})}\frac{1}{2}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u(x)-u(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy-\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}u(x)dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We note that if <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="S3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}(-\Delta)^{s}u_{A}-1=0\ &amp;\hbox{in}~A\\
u_{A}=0&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\setminus A\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}(-\Delta)^{s}u_{A}-1=0\ &amp;\hbox{in}~A\\
u_{A}=0&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\setminus A\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">in the weak sense. It follows that <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{A}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{A}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the corresponding <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> distance between <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\gamma}(A,B):=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}|u_{A}-u_{B}|dx" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\gamma}(A,B):=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}|u_{A}-u_{B}|dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> minimize <math id="S3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(A),E(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(A),E(B)</annotation></semantics></math> respectively and are extended by <math id="S3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We first prove a uniform bound of <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(Symmetric decreasing rearrangement <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.) Let <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(n)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the volume of unit ball in <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the radius <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{f}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{f}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> to be such that</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha(n)R_{f}(y)^{n}=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}\chi_{\{f(x)&gt;y\}}dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(n)R_{f}(y)^{n}=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}\chi_{\{f(x)&gt;y\}}dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We define the symmetrization <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> to be</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}(x)=\sup\{y:R_{f}(y)&gt;|x|\}=\int_{0}^{\infty}\chi_{\{B_{0}(R_{f}(y))\}}(x)dy." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}(x)=\sup\{y:R_{f}(y)&gt;|x|\}=\int_{0}^{\infty}\chi_{\{B_{0}(R_{f}(y))\}}(x)dy.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.7</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(B)\leq E(A)(\leq 0)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:0.389em;" width="0.389em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(B)\leq E(A)(\leq 0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is a ball and <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|B|=|A|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|B|=|A|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be a function that attains the minimum of (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>). Let <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{A}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{A}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be the symmetric rearrangement of <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> defined above, then it follows from Theorem 9.2<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}w_{A}^{*}dx=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}w_{A}dx," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}w_{A}^{*}dx=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}w_{A}dx,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B[w_{A}^{*},w_{A}^{*}]\leq B[w_{A},w_{A}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B[w_{A}^{*},w_{A}^{*}]\leq B[w_{A},w_{A}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(B)\leq\frac{1}{2}B[w_{A}^{*},w_{A}^{*}]-\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}w_{A}^{*}dx\leq\frac{1}{2}B[w_{A},w_{A}]-\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}w_{A}dx=E(A)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(B)\leq\frac{1}{2}B[w_{A}^{*},w_{A}^{*}]-\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}w_{A}^{*}dx\leq\frac{1}{2}B[w_{A},w_{A}]-\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}w_{A}dx=E(A).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3.12</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(A)\leq C|A|^{\frac{n+2s}{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(A)\leq C|A|^{\frac{n+2s}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is known from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> that for any <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the solution of</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}(-\Delta)^{s}u=1\ &amp;\hbox{in}~B_{r}(x_{0})\\
u=0&amp;\hbox{in}~{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\setminus B_{r}(x_{0})\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}(-\Delta)^{s}u=1\ &amp;\hbox{in}~B_{r}(x_{0})\\
u=0&amp;\hbox{in}~{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\setminus B_{r}(x_{0})\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">is given explicitly by</span></p>
<table id="S3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(x)=\frac{2^{-2s}\Gamma(\frac{n}{2})}{\Gamma(\frac{n+2s}{2})\Gamma(1+s)}(r^{2}-|x-x_{0}|^{2})^{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x)=\frac{2^{-2s}\Gamma(\frac{n}{2})}{\Gamma(\frac{n+2s}{2})\Gamma(1+s)}(r^{2}-|x-x_{0}|^{2})^{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, for <math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|B|=Cr^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|B|=Cr^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E(A)|\leq|E(B)|=|\frac{1}{2}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}u|\leq Cr^{n+2s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E(A)|\leq|E(B)|=|\frac{1}{2}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}u|\leq Cr^{n+2s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A|=|B|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A|=|B|</annotation></semantics></math>, the inequality of the Corollary follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.17</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm17.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We say that a measurable set <math id="S3.Thmthm17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> of finite measure is a local shape subsolution for the torsion energy problem (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) if there exists <math id="S3.Thmthm17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for every measurable set <math id="S3.Thmthm17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{A}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S3.Thmthm17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\setminus\tilde{A}|=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\setminus\tilde{A}|=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\gamma}(A,\tilde{A})\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\gamma}(A,\tilde{A})\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="S3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(A)+\Lambda|A|\leq E(\tilde{A})+\Lambda|\tilde{A}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(A)+\Lambda|A|\leq E(\tilde{A})+\Lambda|\tilde{A}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">By an observation of Bucur in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, the <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-minimizer of our problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) is a local subsolution in the sense of above definition. The proof of the following theorem is given in the Appendix.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.19</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S3.Thmthm19.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-minimizer of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>). Then <math id="S3.Thmthm19.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is a local shape subsolution for the torsion energy problem (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The key ingredient in proving the boundedness of subsolutions is the following non-degeneracy lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.20</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S3.Thmthm20.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is a local shape subsolution for the torsion energy problem, let <math id="S3.Thmthm20.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes the torsion energy <math id="S3.Thmthm20.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exists <math id="S3.Thmthm20.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm20.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}=C(n,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}=C(n,s)</annotation></semantics></math>, such that either</span></p>
<table id="S3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{B_{r_{0}}(0)}u\geq C_{0}{r_{0}}^{s}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{B_{r_{0}}(0)}u\geq C_{0}{r_{0}}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm20.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm20.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">or <math id="S3.Thmthm20.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.Thmthm20.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{{r_{0}}/2}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{{r_{0}}/2}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm22" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 3.22</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm22.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The inequality (<a href="#S3.E21" title="In Lemma 3.20. ‣ 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.21</span></a>) can be equivalently written as</p>
<table id="S3.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{B_{r_{0}}(0)}u\geq C(n,s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{B_{r_{0}}(0)}u\geq C(n,s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm22.p1.2" class="ltx_p">since <math id="S3.Thmthm22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed constant on the right hand side of (<a href="#S3.E21" title="In Lemma 3.20. ‣ 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.21</span></a>) and is written in this form for convenience of proof.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth cutoff function such that <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{3r/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{3r/4}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=1</annotation></semantics></math> outside <math id="S3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{9r/10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{9r/10}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\nabla\eta|\leq Cr^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\nabla\eta|\leq Cr^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\eta u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\eta u</annotation></semantics></math> be a competitor of (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>). By (<a href="#S3.E18" title="In Definition 3.17. ‣ 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.18</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Lambda|\{u&gt;0\}\cap B_{3r/4}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Lambda|\{u&gt;0\}\cap B_{3r/4}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq E(A\setminus B_{3r/4})-E(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq E(A\setminus B_{3r/4})-E(A)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3.25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip-36.135pt\leq\frac{1}{2}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(v(x)-v(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}-\frac{(u(x)-u(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy-\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}(v(x)-u(x))dx." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip-36.135pt\leq\frac{1}{2}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(v(x)-v(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}-\frac{(u(x)-u(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}dxdy-\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}(v(x)-u(x))dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">We first estimate the second term,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}(v(x)-u(x))dx\right|=\left|\int_{B_{9r/10}}(\eta(x)-1)u(x)dx\right|\leq Cr^{n}\sup_{B_{r}}u." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></munder><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}}(v(x)-u(x))dx\right|=\left|\int_{B_{9r/10}}(\eta(x)-1)u(x)dx\right|\leq Cr^{n}\sup_{B_{r}}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">For the double integral term, we can split the integral into two pieces,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

