<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S3.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u\|_{L^{\infty}}&lt;C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u\|_{L^{\infty}}&lt;C</annotation></semantics></math> and the second term above can be absorbed by <math id="S3.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> by taking <math id="S3.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> large. Therefore, we have:</span></p>
