<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Existence of Shape Minimizers</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega=B_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega=B_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a ball with radius <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. We first show that <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-minimizers over sets in <math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> exists, and then show that we can take <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. The strategy is to first construct <math id="S4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> as the positivity set of the functions <math id="S4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the minimum below is obtained, and then show that this <math id="S4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-minimizer of problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>). Let</p>
<table id="S4.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\lambda}_{k}=\inf_{u_{i}\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\Omega)}\max_{\alpha\in{\mathbb{R}}^{k}\setminus\{0\}}\left(R[\sum_{1}^{k}\alpha_{i}u_{i}]\ s.t.\ \sum_{1}^{k}|\{u_{i}\neq 0\}|\leq C,(u_{i},u_{j})_{W^{2,s}}=\delta_{ij}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.667em">.</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\lambda}_{k}=\inf_{u_{i}\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\Omega)}\max_{\alpha\in{\mathbb{R}}^{k}\setminus\{0\}}\left(R[\sum_{1}^{k}\alpha_{i}u_{i}]\ s.t.\ \sum_{1}^{k}|\{u_{i}\neq 0\}|\leq C,(u_{i},u_{j})_{W^{2,s}}=\delta_{ij}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda_{k}(A)=\inf_{u_{i}\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\Omega)}\max_{\alpha\in{\mathbb{R}}^{k}\setminus\{0\}}\left(R[\sum_{1}^{k}\alpha_{i}u_{i}]\ s.t.\ u_{i}=0\ a.e.\text{ in }{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\setminus A,(u_{i},u_{j})_{W^{2,s}}=\delta_{ij}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.667em">.</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mtext> in </mtext><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda_{k}(A)=\inf_{u_{i}\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\Omega)}\max_{\alpha\in{\mathbb{R}}^{k}\setminus\{0\}}\left(R[\sum_{1}^{k}\alpha_{i}u_{i}]\ s.t.\ u_{i}=0\ a.e.\text{ in }{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\setminus A,(u_{i},u_{j})_{W^{2,s}}=\delta_{ij}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> is the Rayleigh quotient (<a href="#S2.E9" title="In Notations 2.8. ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The minimum in (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In 4. Existence of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) is attained for some <math id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\Omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\Omega)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{u\neq 0\}|\leq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{u\neq 0\}|\leq C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take a minimizing sequence <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(u^{l})\rightarrow\tilde{\lambda}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(u^{l})\rightarrow\tilde{\lambda}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{l}=\frac{\sum_{1}^{k}\alpha^{l}_{i}u_{i}^{l}}{\|\sum_{1}^{k}\alpha^{l}_{i}u_{i}^{l}\|_{L^{2}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{l}=\frac{\sum_{1}^{k}\alpha^{l}_{i}u_{i}^{l}}{\|\sum_{1}^{k}\alpha^{l}_{i}u_{i}^{l}\|_{L^{2}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(u^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(u^{l})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded, and that <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u^{l}\|_{L^{2}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u^{l}\|_{L^{2}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we know <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{u^{l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{u^{l}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded in <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\Omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\Omega)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{l}\rightarrow u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{l}\rightarrow u</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> weakly in <math id="S4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\Omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\Omega)</annotation></semantics></math>. By compact embedding, <math id="S4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{l}\rightarrow u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{l}\rightarrow u</annotation></semantics></math> strongly in <math id="S4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\Omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\Omega)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, there exists a subsequence <math id="S4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{l}\rightarrow u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{l}\rightarrow u</annotation></semantics></math> pointwise a.e. Since the volume of level sets are lower-semicontinuous with respect to pointwise convergence, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{u&gt;0\}|+|\{u&lt;0\}|\leq\liminf(|\{u^{l}&gt;0\}|+|\{u^{l}&lt;0\}|)\leq C." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{u&gt;0\}|+|\{u&lt;0\}|\leq\liminf(|\{u^{l}&gt;0\}|+|\{u^{l}&lt;0\}|)\leq C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The <math id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-minimizer of problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) exists in the sense of Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm3" title="Definition 2.3. ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega=B_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega=B_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we first show that the minimizer exists over sets contained in <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{R}\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{R}\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{R}=\sum_{1}^{k}\alpha_{i}u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{R}=\sum_{1}^{k}\alpha_{i}u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> where the <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are the minimizers in (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In 4. Existence of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>), and let <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{R}=\{u_{R}\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}=\{u_{R}\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We first observe that <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\lambda}_{k}\leq\lambda_{k}(A_{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\lambda}_{k}\leq\lambda_{k}(A_{R})</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{u:u=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u:u=0</annotation></semantics></math> a.e. in <math id="S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\setminus A_{R}\}\subset\{u:|\{u\neq 0\}|\leq C\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>⊂</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\setminus A_{R}\}\subset\{u:|\{u\neq 0\}|\leq C\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, since the the infimum in (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In 4. Existence of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) is achieved by construction in (<a href="#S4.E2" title="In 4. Existence of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\lambda}_{k}=\lambda_{k}(A_{R})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\lambda}_{k}=\lambda_{k}(A_{R}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">that is, <math id="S4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th eigenvalue of <math id="S4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimizing set.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We’d like to show that as <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the shape minimizer <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> converges in some sense. Indeed, by Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm42" title="Theorem 3.42. ‣ 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.42</span></a> and the remark that follows, we can find <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{R}^{i}\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}({\mathbb{R}}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{R}^{i}\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}({\mathbb{R}}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq k</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{R}=\sum_{i=1}^{k}u_{R}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{R}=\sum_{i=1}^{k}u_{R}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{u_{R_{0}}^{i}\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{R_{0}}^{i}\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{R}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{R}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a translation of <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{R_{0}}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{R_{0}}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{dist}(\{u_{R}^{i}\neq 0\},\{u_{R}^{j}\neq 0\})\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>dist</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{dist}(\{u_{R}^{i}\neq 0\},\{u_{R}^{j}\neq 0\})\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S4.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we consider <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{R_{0}}^{i}\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{R_{0}}^{i}\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}u_{R_{0}}^{i}\subset\mathfrak{S}_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}u_{R_{0}}^{i}\subset\mathfrak{S}_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\{u\neq 0\}\subset\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{u\neq 0\}\subset\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">We observe that <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A_{R})\rightarrow\lambda_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A_{R})\rightarrow\lambda_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A|=|A_{R}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A|=|A_{R}|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We claim that <math id="S4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-minimizer of (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In Definition 2.3. ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>). If not, there exists <math id="S4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}\subset\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}\subset\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A^{\prime}|=|A|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A^{\prime}|=|A|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime})&lt;\lambda_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime})&lt;\lambda_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm42" title="Theorem 3.42. ‣ 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.42</span></a> and the remark that follows, we can find a minimizing sequence <math id="S4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}_{R}=\sum_{i=1}^{k}{u^{\prime}_{R}}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mmultiscripts><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}_{R}=\sum_{i=1}^{k}{u^{\prime}_{R}}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies (1)-(4) above. Let <math id="S4.p6.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A^{\prime}_{R}=\{u^{\prime}_{R}\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}_{R}=\{u^{\prime}_{R}\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime}_{R})\rightarrow\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime})&lt;\lambda_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime}_{R})\rightarrow\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime})&lt;\lambda_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A^{\prime}_{R}|=|A^{\prime}|=|A|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A^{\prime}_{R}|=|A^{\prime}|=|A|</annotation></semantics></math>, but this contradicts the minimality of <math id="S4.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A_{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A_{R})</annotation></semantics></math>, which finished the proof of claim and the theorem.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 4.6</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The argument above doesn’t prove that <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> has finitely many connected pieces, as in each copy or <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, it might happen that <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of infinitely many connected pieces.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
