<p id="S5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k},\cdots,u_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k},\cdots,u_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the corresponding normalized eigenfunctions to <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A),\cdots,\lambda_{1}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A),\cdots,\lambda_{1}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume <math id="S5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> is a free boundary point, that is <math id="S5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\in\partial A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\in\partial A</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="S5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>-harmonic replacement of <math id="S5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> on the ball <math id="S5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> and that <math id="S5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|B_{r}(0)\cap A^{C}|\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|B_{r}(0)\cap A^{C}|\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, that is,</p>
