<p id="S5.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is the Rayleigh quotient (<a href="#S2.E9" title="In Notations 2.8. ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.9</span></a>), and the max is achieved at <math id="S5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\alpha}+tw_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\alpha}+tw_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j},j=k-l+1,\cdots,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j},j=k-l+1,\cdots,k</annotation></semantics></math>, since it is orthogonal to <math id="S5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1},...,u_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1},...,u_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We first claim that for any <math id="S5.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> small,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
