<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq B[u_{\alpha}+tw_{\alpha},u_{\alpha}+tw_{\alpha}]+Cr^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq B[u_{\alpha}+tw_{\alpha},u_{\alpha}+tw_{\alpha}]+Cr^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=B[u_{\alpha},u_{\alpha}]+2tB[u_{\alpha},w_{\alpha}]+t^{2}B[w_{\alpha},w_{\alpha}]+Cr^{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=B[u_{\alpha},u_{\alpha}]+2tB[u_{\alpha},w_{\alpha}]+t^{2}B[w_{\alpha},w_{\alpha}]+Cr^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">Here we move the term linear in <math id="S5.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> to the left. Since <math id="S5.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, divide by <math id="S5.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-t</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S5.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B[u_{\alpha},w_{\alpha}]\leq|t|B[w_{\alpha},w_{\alpha}]+C\frac{r^{n}}{|t|}\leq C_{1}(\alpha)|t|B[w,w]+C\frac{r^{n}}{|t|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B[u_{\alpha},w_{\alpha}]\leq|t|B[w_{\alpha},w_{\alpha}]+C\frac{r^{n}}{|t|}\leq C_{1}(\alpha)|t|B[w,w]+C\frac{r^{n}}{|t|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}(\alpha)=\max\alpha_{j}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}(\alpha)=\max\alpha_{j}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We observe that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B[u_{\alpha},w_{\alpha}]=B[u_{\alpha},\sum_{j=k-l+1}^{k}\alpha_{k}\tilde{w}_{j}+\sum_{i=1}^{k-1}\textit{Proj}_{\mathbf{u_{i}}}{w}]\geq B[u_{\alpha},C_{2}(\alpha)w]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Proj</mtext><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐢</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B[u_{\alpha},w_{\alpha}]=B[u_{\alpha},\sum_{j=k-l+1}^{k}\alpha_{k}\tilde{w}_{j}+\sum_{i=1}^{k-1}\textit{Proj}_{\mathbf{u_{i}}}{w}]\geq B[u_{\alpha},C_{2}(\alpha)w]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p2.12.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}(\alpha)=\{\min\alpha_{j}^{2}|\alpha_{j}\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}(\alpha)=\{\min\alpha_{j}^{2}|\alpha_{j}\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S5.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal to <math id="S5.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1},...,u_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1},...,u_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, since <math id="S5.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=h-u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=h-u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, integration by part gives <math id="S5.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B[h,w]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B[h,w]=0</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S5.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>-harmonic. Therefore, <math id="S5.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B[u_{\alpha},w]=B[w,w]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B[u_{\alpha},w]=B[w,w]</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href="#S5.E12" title="In Proof. ‣ 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.12</span></a>) becomes</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}B[w,w]\leq C_{1}|t|B[w,w]+C\frac{r^{n}}{|t|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}B[w,w]\leq C_{1}|t|B[w,w]+C\frac{r^{n}}{|t|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p2.13.1" class="ltx_text">Now choosing <math id="S5.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|t|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|t|</annotation></semantics></math> small yields</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B[w,w]\leq Cr^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B[w,w]\leq Cr^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p2.14.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 5.13</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 5.4. ‣ 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a> shows one main difficulty in studying spectral minimizers as the estimates depend on a linear combination of <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k},\cdots,u_{k-l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k},\cdots,u_{k-l}</annotation></semantics></math> instead on a function <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. How to recover some information on <math id="S5.Thmthm13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> from estimates on the linear combination remains unknown.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A immediate corollary is that</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 5.14</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S5.Thmthm14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is simple with corresponding eigenfunction <math id="S5.Thmthm14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B[u_{k}-h,u_{k}-h]\leq Cr^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B[u_{k}-h,u_{k}-h]\leq Cr^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To prove the optimal regularity, we do extensions as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> and reformulate the fractional Laplacian in <math id="S5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math> dimension.
For <math id="S5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="S5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=(x^{\prime},y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=(x^{\prime},y)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}\in\tilde{W}^{2,s}({\mathbb{R}}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}\in\tilde{W}^{2,s}({\mathbb{R}}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as the following. First, for <math id="S5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="S5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> to be the solution of</p>
<table id="S5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}{\rm div}(y^{a}\nabla f)=0&amp;\hbox{in}~y&gt;0,\\
f(x,0)=f^{\prime}(x)&amp;\hbox{on}~y=0.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>on</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}{\rm div}(y^{a}\nabla f)=0&amp;\hbox{in}~y&gt;0,\\
f(x,0)=f^{\prime}(x)&amp;\hbox{on}~y=0.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=1-2s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=1-2s</annotation></semantics></math>. We then extent <math id="S5.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> to the whole <math id="S5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> by setting <math id="S5.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,-y)=f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,-y)=f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">By this construction, we can define extension of <math id="S5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> by doing the extension in every copy of <math id="S5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, for any <math id="S5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S5.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\sum_{i=1}^{k}g," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\sum_{i=1}^{k}g,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is the extension of <math id="S5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{f^{\prime}|_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{f^{\prime}|_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}_{i}}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> defined above.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, it is known that for <math id="S5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}\in\tilde{W}^{2,s}({\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}\in\tilde{W}^{2,s}({\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}})</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> the its extension, then</p>
<table id="S5.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u^{\prime}(x)-u^{\prime}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k}}|x_{n+1}|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}dx," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{(u^{\prime}(x)-u^{\prime}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}=\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k}}|x_{n+1}|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}dx,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">and thus problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) is equivalent to minimizing the following functional in the extended domain</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S5.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k}}|x_{n+1}|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}}{\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times\{0\}}|u|^{2}}+\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times\{0\}}\chi_{\{u&gt;0\}}+\chi_{\{u&lt;0\}}\ d\mathcal{H}^{n-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>χ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>χ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k}}|x_{n+1}|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}}{\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times\{0\}}|u|^{2}}+\int_{\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times\{0\}}\chi_{\{u&gt;0\}}+\chi_{\{u&lt;0\}}\ d\mathcal{H}^{n-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to be the even extension of <math id="S5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> in Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 5.4. ‣ 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p10.1" class="ltx_p">By extension, we automatically have <math id="S5.p10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm div}(y^{a}\nabla u)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm div}(y^{a}\nabla u)=0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n+1}\setminus(\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}\times\{0\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n+1}\setminus(\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}\times\{0\})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p11.1" class="ltx_p">We define the following space for <math id="S5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subset\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subset\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
