<div id="S5.Thmthm17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.17</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.Thmthm17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a><span id="S5.Thmthm17.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">]</span></cite><span id="S5.Thmthm17.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
If <math id="S5.Thmthm17.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm div}(|y|^{a}\nabla{h})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm div}(|y|^{a}\nabla{h})=0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.Thmthm17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{R}(x^{\prime},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{R}(x^{\prime},0)</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S5.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{r^{n+1+a}}\int_{B_{r}(x^{\prime},0)}|y|^{a}|\nabla h|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{r^{n+1+a}}\int_{B_{r}(x^{\prime},0)}|y|^{a}|\nabla h|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm17.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm17.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is monotone increasing in <math id="S5.Thmthm17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.Thmthm17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;R</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The following optimal regularity uses technique similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. The proof is provided in the appendix for completeness.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.19</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmthm19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> be as in Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 5.4. ‣ 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a> and <math id="S5.Thmthm19.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> its extension in <math id="S5.Thmthm19.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.Thmthm19.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C^{0,s}(\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C^{0,s}(\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n+1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p13.1" class="ltx_p">One immediate consequence is that the <math id="S5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-minimizers are open.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 5.20</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmthm20.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S5.Thmthm20.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-minimizer of (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>), then <math id="S5.Thmthm20.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> has an open representative.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p14.1" class="ltx_p">We assume henceforth that the minimizing eigenvalue <math id="S5.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) is simple.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm21" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 5.21</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm21.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm21.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm21.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmthm21.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u_{p}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{p}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence minimizers of (<a href="#S5.E15" title="In 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.15</span></a>) with <math id="S5.Thmthm21.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u_{p}\|_{L^{\infty}(\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}\times\{0\})}\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u_{p}\|_{L^{\infty}(\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}\times\{0\})}\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>. Then There exists a subsequence and a function <math id="S5.Thmthm21.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for any open <math id="S5.Thmthm21.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subset\subset\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subset\subset\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<ol id="S5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}\in H^{1}(a,U)\cup C^{s}(\overline{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}\in H^{1}(a,U)\cup C^{s}(\overline{U})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{p}\rightarrow u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{p}\rightarrow u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for </span><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&lt;s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&lt;s</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{p}\rightarrow u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{p}\rightarrow u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(a,U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(a,U)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> weakly.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u_{p}\|_{L^{\infty}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u_{p}\|_{L^{\infty}}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly bounded, (1),(2) follows from Holder regularity. (3) follows from (<a href="#Sx2.E29" title="In Proof. ‣ 10.2. Proof of theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.29</span></a>) in the proof of above Theorem in Appendix and Sobolev inequality.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm22" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 5.22</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm22.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.Thmthm22.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a><span id="S5.Thmthm22.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">]</span></cite><span id="S5.Thmthm22.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Let <math id="S5.Thmthm22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> be a minimizer of (<a href="#S5.E15" title="In 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.15</span></a>), for any ball <math id="S5.Thmthm22.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\subset\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\subset\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S5.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5.23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{B}|x|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}=\int_{\partial B}|x_{n}|^{a}uu_{\nu}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{B}|x|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}=\int_{\partial B}|x_{n}|^{a}uu_{\nu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm24" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_notn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notation 5.24</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm24.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm24.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any set <math id="S5.Thmthm24.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.Thmthm24.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote <math id="S5.Thmthm24.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}=D|_{x_{n+1}=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}=D|_{x_{n+1}=0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a function <math id="S5.Thmthm24.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:{\mathbb{R}}^{n+1}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, denote <math id="S5.Thmthm24.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}=f|_{x_{n+1}=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}=f|_{x_{n+1}=0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6. </span>Non-degeneracy</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to do blow up analysis, it is not a priori known that the blow up limit is non zero, so we need a lower bound for eigenfunctions. We note that in Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm19" title="Theorem 5.19. ‣ 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.19</span></a>, we only proved that some of the eigenfunctions are Hölder continuous. It is not known that the eigenfunctions that are Hölder continuous being non-degenerate. To overcome this issue, we henceforth assume that the <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th eigenvalue is simple. In this case, <math id="S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is Hölder continuous, and we proceed to show a lower bound for <math id="S6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.1</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|B_{r/8}(x_{0})\cap A|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|B_{r/8}(x_{0})\cap A|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{B_{r}(x_{0})}|u_{k}|\geq c_{0}r^{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{B_{r}(x_{0})}|u_{k}|\geq c_{0}r^{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By translating, assume <math id="S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose for contradiction that <math id="S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{B_{r_{0}}(0)}u\leq c_{0}r^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{B_{r_{0}}(0)}u\leq c_{0}r^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, we claim that <math id="S6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall z\in B_{1/4}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall z\in B_{1/4}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S6.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6.2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{B_{r/4}(z)}|u_{k}|\leq\frac{c_{0}r^{s}}{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{B_{r/4}(z)}|u_{k}|\leq\frac{c_{0}r^{s}}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the claim inductively to balls of radius <math id="S6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{-i}r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{-i}r</annotation></semantics></math> centered on each <math id="S6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in B_{1/4}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in B_{1/4}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="S6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|u_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|u_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes on <math id="S6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r/4}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a contradiction. Now we proceed to the proof of claim.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Cacciopoli’s inequality (<a href="#S2.E17" title="In Lemma 2.15. ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.17</span></a>) implies</span></p>
<table id="S6.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6.3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{B_{9/10r}}\int_{B_{9/10r}}\frac{(u_{k}(x)-u_{k}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}&lt;Cc_{0}r^{s}r^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{B_{9/10r}}\int_{B_{9/10r}}\frac{(u_{k}(x)-u_{k}(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}&lt;Cc_{0}r^{s}r^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, take <math id="S6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}=A\setminus B_{3r/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}=A\setminus B_{3r/4}</annotation></semantics></math> as a competitor for <math id="S6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\cap B_{3r/4}|\leq\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime})-\lambda_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\cap B_{3r/4}|\leq\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime})-\lambda_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking <math id="S6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> to be <math id="S6.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> outside <math id="S6.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{9r/10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{9r/10}</annotation></semantics></math>, vanishes on <math id="S6.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{3r/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{3r/4}</annotation></semantics></math>, and has the derivative bounded by <math id="S6.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Cr^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Cr^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S6.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{j}=\varphi u_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{j}=\varphi u_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,2,...,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,2,...,k</annotation></semantics></math>. We wish to control <math id="S6.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}|v_{k}-u_{k}|^{2}=\int_{B_{9r/10}}|v_{k}-u_{k}|^{2}\leq C\int_{B_{9r/10}}|u_{k}|^{2}\leq Cc_{0}^{2}r^{2s}r^{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}|v_{k}-u_{k}|^{2}=\int_{B_{9r/10}}|v_{k}-u_{k}|^{2}\leq C\int_{B_{9r/10}}|u_{k}|^{2}\leq Cc_{0}^{2}r^{2s}r^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We claim that we have</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6.4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{((u_{k}-v_{k})(x)-(u_{k}-v_{k})(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}\leq Cc_{0}r^{s}r^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{((u_{k}-v_{k})(x)-(u_{k}-v_{k})(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}\leq Cc_{0}r^{s}r^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">To prove it, we break the integral, similar to before, into the following:</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}=\int_{B_{9r/10}}\int_{B_{9r/10}}+2\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\setminus B_{9r/10}}\int_{B_{9r/10}}:=I+II." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.111em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}=\int_{B_{9r/10}}\int_{B_{9r/10}}+2\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\setminus B_{9r/10}}\int_{B_{9r/10}}:=I+II.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">and we estimate</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\int_{B_{9r/10}}\int_{B_{9r/10}}\frac{(u_{k}(x)-u_{k}(y))^{2}+(v_{k}(x)-v_{k}(y)^{2}))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\int_{B_{9r/10}}\int_{B_{9r/10}}\frac{(u_{k}(x)-u_{k}(y))^{2}+(v_{k}(x)-v_{k}(y)^{2}))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq Cc_{0}^{2}r^{2s}r^{n}+C\int_{B_{9r/10}}\int_{B_{9r/10}}\frac{(v_{k}(x)-v_{k}(y)^{2}))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq Cc_{0}^{2}r^{2s}r^{n}+C\int_{B_{9r/10}}\int_{B_{9r/10}}\frac{(v_{k}(x)-v_{k}(y)^{2}))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6.7)</span></td>
