<div id="S6.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We notice that <math id="S6.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are not necessarily orthogonal and thus we need to orthogonalize <math id="S6.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s and we claim that the resulting <math id="S6.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> also satisfy the inequality (<a href="#S6.E21" title="In Proof. ‣ 6. Non-degeneracy ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.21</span></a>). Let <math id="S6.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{k}=v_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{k}=v_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, then define</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
