<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p11.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p11.10.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, take any <math id="S6.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in B_{r/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in B_{r/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, using (<a href="#S3.E34" title="In Proof. ‣ 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.34</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

