<div id="S7.Thmthm29" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 7.29</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm29.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm29.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm29.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm29.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}=\frac{u(rx)}{r^{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}=\frac{u(rx)}{r^{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S7.Thmthm29.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(1,u_{r})=W(r,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(1,u_{r})=W(r,u)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">One important consequence of the above almost monotonicity formula is that it shows that the blow up, defined as the limit of</p>
<table id="S7.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}=\frac{u(rx)}{r^{s}}\rightarrow u_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}=\frac{u(rx)}{r^{s}}\rightarrow u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p3.2" class="ltx_p">is homogeneous of degree <math id="S7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. We first show that <math id="S7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy a PDE on the compliment of <math id="S7.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(u)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm30" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.30</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm30.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}\rightarrow u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}\rightarrow u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a blow up, we have</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm div}(y^{a}\nabla u_{0})=0\text{ in }\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k}\setminus\{y=0\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> in </mtext><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm div}(y^{a}\nabla u_{0})=0\text{ in }\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k}\setminus\{y=0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S7.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}\rightarrow u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}\rightarrow u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S7.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(a,U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(a,U)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="S7.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm div}(y^{a}\nabla u_{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm div}(y^{a}\nabla u_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S7.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k}\setminus\{y=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k}\setminus\{y=0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the thin space <math id="S7.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\Delta)^{s}u_{k}=\lambda_{k}u_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\Delta)^{s}u_{k}=\lambda_{k}u_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(-\Delta)^{s}u_{k}=-\lim_{y\rightarrow 0}y^{a}\partial_{y}u(x,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\Delta)^{s}u_{k}=-\lim_{y\rightarrow 0}y^{a}\partial_{y}u(x,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">So <math id="S7.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\Delta)^{s}u_{r}^{\prime}=r^{2s}\lambda_{k}u_{r}^{\prime}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\Delta)^{s}u_{r}^{\prime}=r^{2s}\lambda_{k}u_{r}^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S7.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}^{\prime}\rightarrow u_{0}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}^{\prime}\rightarrow u_{0}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly locally, we have <math id="S7.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\Delta)^{s}u_{0}^{\prime}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\Delta)^{s}u_{0}^{\prime}=0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S7.p4.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{u_{0}^{\prime}\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{0}^{\prime}\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\lim_{y\rightarrow 0}y^{a}\partial_{y}u_{0}(x,y)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\lim_{y\rightarrow 0}y^{a}\partial_{y}u_{0}(x,y)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">So, the even reflection satisfies <math id="S7.p4.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm div}(y^{a}\nabla u_{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm div}(y^{a}\nabla u_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S7.p4.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}\times\{0\}\cap\{u_{0}\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}\times\{0\}\cap\{u_{0}\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math> (by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> Lemma 4.1).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm31" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 7.31</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm31.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}\rightarrow u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}\rightarrow u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a blow up at <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{0},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{0},0)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is homogeneous of degree <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#Sx2.E29" title="In Proof. ‣ 10.2. Proof of theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.29</span></a>) and optimal regularity, <math id="S7.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(0+,u,x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(0+,u,x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded from below.
We claim that</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(r,u)=W(1,u_{r})\rightarrow W(1,u_{0})=W(0,u_{r})=L." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(r,u)=W(1,u_{r})\rightarrow W(1,u_{0})=W(0,u_{r})=L.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S7.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7.32)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W(1,u_{0})=\frac{1}{r^{n}}\left(\int_{B_{1}}|y|^{a}|\nabla u_{0}|^{2}+\int_{B_{1}^{\prime}}\chi_{\{u_{0}\neq 0\}}\right)-\frac{s}{r^{n-1}}\int_{\partial B_{1}}|y|^{a}u_{0}^{2}=L." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">+</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi></msup><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(1,u_{0})=\frac{1}{r^{n}}\left(\int_{B_{1}}|y|^{a}|\nabla u_{0}|^{2}+\int_{B_{1}^{\prime}}\chi_{\{u_{0}\neq 0\}}\right)-\frac{s}{r^{n-1}}\int_{\partial B_{1}}|y|^{a}u_{0}^{2}=L.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">We first note that if the claim is true, then the above equation grantees that <math id="S7.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is homogeneous of degree <math id="S7.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. We proceed to the proof of the claim.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="S7.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S7.E2" title="In Theorem 7.1. ‣ 7. Blow-up Analysis ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>) we wish to show that the three terms converge to the corresponding limit respectively. By Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmthm21" title="Corollary 5.21. ‣ 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.21</span></a>, the third term converges to the corresponding term in (<a href="#S7.E32" title="In Proof. ‣ 7. Blow-up Analysis ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.32</span></a>).
For the first term, let <math id="S7.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in C_{c}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in C_{c}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S7.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a sequence <math id="S7.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\rightarrow 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\rightarrow 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S7.p6.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{u_{0}\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{0}\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a neighborhood of supp <math id="S7.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int|y|^{a}|\nabla u_{0}|^{2}=\lim_{\epsilon\rightarrow 0}\int|y|^{a}\nabla u_{0}\nabla(u_{0}-\epsilon)_{+}\eta=-\lim_{\epsilon\rightarrow 0}\int|y|^{a}(u_{0}-\epsilon)_{+}\nabla\eta\nabla u_{0}=-\int|y|^{a}u_{0}\nabla\eta\nabla u_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mi>η</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi></msup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi></msup><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int|y|^{a}|\nabla u_{0}|^{2}=\lim_{\epsilon\rightarrow 0}\int|y|^{a}\nabla u_{0}\nabla(u_{0}-\epsilon)_{+}\eta=-\lim_{\epsilon\rightarrow 0}\int|y|^{a}(u_{0}-\epsilon)_{+}\nabla\eta\nabla u_{0}=-\int|y|^{a}u_{0}\nabla\eta\nabla u_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first and last equality follows from dominated convergence theorem, and the second equality uses integration by part with respect to the measure <math id="S7.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|y|^{a}dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|y|^{a}dx</annotation></semantics></math> and that <math id="S7.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is harmonic on <math id="S7.p6.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{u_{0}&gt;\epsilon\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{0}&gt;\epsilon\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that above calculation also works if we replace <math id="S7.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S7.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int|y|^{a}|\nabla u_{0}|^{2}=-\int|y|^{a}u_{0}\nabla\eta\nabla u_{0}=-\lim_{r\rightarrow 0}|y|^{a}u_{r}\nabla\eta\nabla u_{r}=\lim_{r\rightarrow 0}\int|\nabla u_{r}|^{2}\eta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int|y|^{a}|\nabla u_{0}|^{2}=-\int|y|^{a}u_{0}\nabla\eta\nabla u_{0}=-\lim_{r\rightarrow 0}|y|^{a}u_{r}\nabla\eta\nabla u_{r}=\lim_{r\rightarrow 0}\int|\nabla u_{r}|^{2}\eta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that <math id="S7.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}\rightarrow u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}\rightarrow u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S7.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}_{\text{loc}}(a,U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mtext>loc</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}_{\text{loc}}(a,U)</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{B_{1}}|y|^{a}|\nabla u_{r}|^{2}\rightarrow\int_{B_{1}}|y|^{a}|\nabla u_{0}|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{B_{1}}|y|^{a}|\nabla u_{r}|^{2}\rightarrow\int_{B_{1}}|y|^{a}|\nabla u_{0}|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is left to check that</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{B_{r}^{\prime}}\chi_{\{u_{r}\neq 0\}}\rightarrow\int_{B_{1}^{\prime}}\chi_{\{u_{0}\neq 0\}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mi>χ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mi>χ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{B_{r}^{\prime}}\chi_{\{u_{r}\neq 0\}}\rightarrow\int_{B_{1}^{\prime}}\chi_{\{u_{0}\neq 0\}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">First we note that <math id="S7.p8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1_{\{u_{r}&gt;0\}}\leq 1_{\{u_{0}&gt;0\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1_{\{u_{r}&gt;0\}}\leq 1_{\{u_{0}&gt;0\}}</annotation></semantics></math> by lower semi-continuity and <math id="S7.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> convergence (Prop <a href="#S5.Thmthm21" title="Corollary 5.21. ‣ 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.21</span></a>). We proceed to check the other inequality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S7.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> be such that <math id="S7.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and there exists a sequence <math id="S7.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{r}\rightarrow x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{r}\rightarrow x</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S7.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}(x_{r})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}(x_{r})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="S7.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="S7.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S7.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{r}\in B_{\epsilon}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{r}\in B_{\epsilon}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S7.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}_{r}(y_{r})\geq c\epsilon^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}_{r}(y_{r})\geq c\epsilon^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S7.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\rightarrow u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\rightarrow u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly in compact sets, we have <math id="S7.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{r}\rightarrow y_{0}\in B_{\epsilon}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{r}\rightarrow y_{0}\in B_{\epsilon}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S7.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}_{0}(y_{0})\geq c\epsilon^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}_{0}(y_{0})\geq c\epsilon^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, by Hölder continuity, there exists <math id="S7.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\delta\epsilon}(y_{0})\subset B_{\epsilon}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\delta\epsilon}(y_{0})\subset B_{\epsilon}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S7.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}_{0}(B_{\delta\epsilon}(y_{0}))\geq c\epsilon^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}_{0}(B_{\delta\epsilon}(y_{0}))\geq c\epsilon^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This implies that</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sup_{B_{\epsilon}(x)}u^{\prime}_{0}&gt;C\epsilon^{s},\text{ and }|\{u_{0}&gt;0\}\cup B_{r}|&gt;Cr^{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{B_{\epsilon}(x)}u^{\prime}_{0}&gt;C\epsilon^{s},\text{ and }|\{u_{0}&gt;0\}\cup B_{r}|&gt;Cr^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">that is, <math id="S7.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is in the measure theoretic closure of <math id="S7.p9.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\{u^{\prime}_{0}&gt;0\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\{u^{\prime}_{0}&gt;0\}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lebesgue density theorem, the measure theoretic boundary satisfies <math id="S7.p9.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\partial_{*}\{u^{\prime}_{0}&gt;0\}|=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><mo>∗</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\partial_{*}\{u^{\prime}_{0}&gt;0\}|=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The case where <math id="S7.p9.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x\in\{u_{0}&lt;0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\{u_{0}&lt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math> follows from the same argument and the claim follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8. </span>Separation of the Free Boundary and Density Estimates</h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have established that if the minimizing eigenvalue <math id="S8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> of problem (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) is simple, then the corresponding eigenfunction <math id="S8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0,s}</annotation></semantics></math> and non-degenerate. In this section we follow the idea of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> to show that the free boundary is separated.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the corresponding eigenfunction to <math id="S8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(x,y)=u(x_{1},\cdots,x_{n},y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x,y)=u(x_{1},\cdots,x_{n},y)</annotation></semantics></math> be the extension of <math id="S8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}\rightarrow u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}\rightarrow u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a blow up of <math id="S8.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p>
<table id="S8.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8.1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Lambda(u)=\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times\{0\}\cap\{u=0\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(u)=\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\times\{0\}\cap\{u=0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8.2</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a><span id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">]</span></cite><span id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Let <math id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> be homogeneous of degree <math id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> with nontrivial positive and negative parts, continuous, and satisfies <math id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm div}(|y|^{a}\nabla u)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm div}(|y|^{a}\nabla u)=0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k}\setminus\Lambda(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}^{n+1}_{k}\setminus\Lambda(u)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;\min\{1,1-a\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;\min\{1,1-a\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 8.3</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-minimizer, <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the corresponding eigenfunction. Then</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial\{u_{k}(x)&gt;0\}\cap\partial\{u_{k}(x)&lt;0\}=\varnothing." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">∩</mo><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\{u_{k}(x)&gt;0\}\cap\partial\{u_{k}(x)&lt;0\}=\varnothing.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is not sign changing, the theorem is trivially true. Assume <math id="S8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> has both nontrial positive and negative part. Suppose by contradiction, there exists <math id="S8.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{0}\in\partial\{u_{k}(x)&gt;0\}\cap\partial\{u_{k}(x)&lt;0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">∩</mo><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\partial\{u_{k}(x)&gt;0\}\cap\partial\{u_{k}(x)&lt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S8.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}=u(rx)/r^{s}\rightarrow u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}=u(rx)/r^{s}\rightarrow u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a blow up. Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm30" title="Lemma 7.30. ‣ 7. Blow-up Analysis ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.30</span></a> shows that <math id="S8.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm div}(|y|^{a}\nabla u_{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm div}(|y|^{a}\nabla u_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. By the lower bound in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm42" title="Theorem 3.42. ‣ 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.42</span></a> and <math id="S8.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> convergence, <math id="S8.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> has non-trivial positive and negative parts. By Corollary <a href="#S7.Thmthm31" title="Corollary 7.31. ‣ 7. Blow-up Analysis ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.31</span></a>, <math id="S8.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is homogeneous of degree <math id="S8.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=(1-a)/2&lt;\min\{1,1-a\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=(1-a)/2&lt;\min\{1,1-a\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This contradicts above lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p4.1" class="ltx_p">It follows that we have the following density estimates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 8.4</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-minimizer, <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the normalized corresponding eigenfunction. Suppose <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is a free boundary point, that is <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in\partial A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\partial A</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, there exists <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> small, we have</span></p>
<table id="S8.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8.5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{u_{k}&gt;0\}\cap B_{r}(x_{0})|\geq Cr^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{u_{k}&gt;0\}\cap B_{r}(x_{0})|\geq Cr^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S8.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8.6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{u_{k}=0\}\cap B_{r}(x_{0})|\geq Cr^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{u_{k}=0\}\cap B_{r}(x_{0})|\geq Cr^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> has no cusps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">First we note that (<a href="#S8.E5" title="In Theorem 8.4. ‣ 8. Separation of the Free Boundary and Density Estimates ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.5</span></a>) follows directly from optimal regularity and nondegeneracy. By Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 6.1. ‣ 6. Non-degeneracy ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>, there exists <math id="S8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in B_{r/2}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in B_{r/2}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S8.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(y)\geq c(r/2)^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(y)\geq c(r/2)^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S8.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C^{0,s}(B_{r}(x_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C^{0,s}(B_{r}(x_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S8.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S8.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S8.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{cr}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{cr}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Cr^{n}=|B_{cr}(y)|\leq|B_{r}(x_{0})\cap\{u&gt;0\}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Cr^{n}=|B_{cr}(y)|\leq|B_{r}(x_{0})\cap\{u&gt;0\}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed to prove (<a href="#S8.E6" title="In Theorem 8.4. ‣ 8. Separation of the Free Boundary and Density Estimates ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.6</span></a>). Without loss on generality, suppose <math id="S8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S8.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r}(0)\cap A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}(0)\cap A</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose for contradiction,</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|B_{r}(0)\cap A_{i}^{C}|=o(r^{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|B_{r}(0)\cap A_{i}^{C}|=o(r^{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S8.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="S8.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>-harmonic replacement of <math id="S8.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S8.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>, that is</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}(-\Delta)^{s}h=0\ &amp;\hbox{in}~B_{r}=B_{r}(0),\\
h=u&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\setminus B_{r}(0),\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}(-\Delta)^{s}h=0\ &amp;\hbox{in}~B_{r}=B_{r}(0),\\
h=u&amp;\hbox{in}~\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k}\setminus B_{r}(0),\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="S8.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}-h\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}_{0}(B_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}-h\in\tilde{W}^{s,2}_{0}(B_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> as a text function, we have</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8.7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B[h,u_{k}-h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B[h,u_{k}-h]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{R}^{n}_{k}}\frac{(h(x)-h(y))((u_{k}-h)(x)-(u_{k}-h)(y))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{R}^{n}_{k}}\frac{(h(x)-h(y))((u_{k}-h)(x)-(u_{k}-h)(y))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8.8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B[u_{k},u_{k}-h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B[u_{k},u_{k}-h]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{{R}^{n}_{k}}\int_{{R}^{n}_{k}}\frac{(u_{k}(x)-u_{k}(y))((u-h)(x)-(u_{k}-h)(y))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{{R}^{n}_{k}}\int_{{R}^{n}_{k}}\frac{(u_{k}(x)-u_{k}(y))((u-h)(x)-(u_{k}-h)(y))}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B_{r}}\lambda_{k}u_{k}(u_{k}-h)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B_{r}}\lambda_{k}u_{k}(u_{k}-h).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">We first note that <math id="S8.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&lt;u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&lt;u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> by strong maximum principle <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> and thus <math id="S8.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{k}-h&gt;C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{k}-h&gt;C</annotation></semantics></math> in any compact set in <math id="S8.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also by assumption, <math id="S8.p6.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{u_{k}&gt;0\}\cap B_{r}(0)|=Cr^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{u_{k}&gt;0\}\cap B_{r}(0)|=Cr^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{B_{r}}\lambda_{k}u_{k}(u_{k}-h)\geq C\lambda_{k}\int_{\{u_{k}&gt;0\}\cap B_{r}}u_{k}&gt;Cr^{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>∩</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{B_{r}}\lambda_{k}u_{k}(u_{k}-h)\geq C\lambda_{k}\int_{\{u_{k}&gt;0\}\cap B_{r}}u_{k}&gt;Cr^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">and that</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B[u_{k},u_{k}]-B[h,h]=B[u_{k},u_{k}-h]+B[h,u_{k}-h]&gt;Cr^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B[u_{k},u_{k}]-B[h,h]=B[u_{k},u_{k}-h]+B[h,u_{k}-h]&gt;Cr^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p6.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p6.6.1" class="ltx_text">We also have that</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|h\|_{L^{2}}^{2}=\|u\|_{L^{2}}^{2}+\int_{B_{r}}h^{2}-\int_{B_{r}}u^{2}\geq\|u\|_{L^{2}}^{2}-Cr^{n+2s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|h\|_{L^{2}}^{2}=\|u\|_{L^{2}}^{2}+\int_{B_{r}}h^{2}-\int_{B_{r}}u^{2}\geq\|u\|_{L^{2}}^{2}-Cr^{n+2s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p6.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p6.7.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality uses <math id="S8.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C^{0,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C^{0,s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R[h]-R[u_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R[h]-R[u_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
