<section id="Sx2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendix</h2>

<section id="Sx2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">10.1. </span>proof of theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm19" title="Theorem 3.19. ‣ 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.19</span></a>.</h3>

<div id="Sx2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the convenience of the reader, we include the proof of theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm19" title="Theorem 3.19. ‣ 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.19</span></a>, which follows the argument given in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.Thmthm18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Sx2.Thmthm18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 10.18</span></span><span id="Sx2.Thmthm18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Sx2.Thmthm18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.Thmthm18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.Thmthm18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Sx2.Thmthm18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathfrak{S}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathfrak{S}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Sx2.Thmthm18.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A=\{u\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\{u\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for every <math id="Sx2.Thmthm18.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="Sx2.Thmthm18.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> depending only on <math id="Sx2.Thmthm18.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> such that for every <math id="Sx2.Thmthm18.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leq k</annotation></semantics></math> and for every <math id="Sx2.Thmthm18.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathfrak{S}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathfrak{S}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Sx2.Thmthm18.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B=\{v\neq 0\}\subset A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\{v\neq 0\}\subset A</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(A)}-\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(B)}\right|\leq c_{k}(A)d_{\gamma}(A,B)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(A)}-\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(B)}\right|\leq c_{k}(A)d_{\gamma}(A,B).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Sx2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="Sx2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider the linear subspace <math id="Sx2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{k}\subset L^{2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{k}\subset L^{2}(\mathcal{R}^{n}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the first <math id="Sx2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> eigenfunctions of the Dirichlet fractional Laplacian on <math id="Sx2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="Sx2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite dimensional subspace of <math id="Sx2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{S}}_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{S}}_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote by <math id="Sx2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{A}:L^{2}(A)\rightarrow L^{2}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{A}:L^{2}(A)\rightarrow L^{2}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> the resolvent operator ie. <math id="Sx2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A)f=u_{f,A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A)f=u_{f,A}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Sx2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\Delta)^{s}u_{A,f}=f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\Delta)^{s}u_{A,f}=f</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We set <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k}:L^{2}(A)\rightarrow V_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k}:L^{2}(A)\rightarrow V_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> the <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> projection on <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and define the finite rank, positive, self adjoint operators:</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{k}^{A}=P_{k}\circ R_{A}\circ P_{k},\ T_{k}^{B}=P_{k}\circ R_{B}\circ P_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{k}^{A}=P_{k}\circ R_{A}\circ P_{k},\ T_{k}^{B}=P_{k}\circ R_{B}\circ P_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Denoting <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{A}),\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{A}),\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{B})</annotation></semantics></math> the <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>th eigenvalues of the operators <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{k}^{A},T_{k}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{k}^{A},T_{k}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{B})\leq\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(B)},\ \mu_{j}(T_{k}^{A})=\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(A)}\ \forall j=1,2,...,k." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{B})\leq\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(B)},\ \mu_{j}(T_{k}^{A})=\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(A)}\ \forall j=1,2,...,k.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, for every <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{B})=\mu_{j}(P_{k}\circ R_{A}\circ P_{k})=\mu_{j}(P_{k})^{2}\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(B)}\leq\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(B)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{B})=\mu_{j}(P_{k}\circ R_{A}\circ P_{k})=\mu_{j}(P_{k})^{2}\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(B)}\leq\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(B)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{j}(P_{k})\leq\mu_{1}(P_{k})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{j}(P_{k})\leq\mu_{1}(P_{k})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. In the same way, we have:</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{A})\leq\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(A)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{A})\leq\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(A)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, let <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>th eigenfunction of <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> associated with <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{j}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{j}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that:</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{k}^{A}u_{j}=P_{k}\circ R_{A}\circ P_{k}u_{j}=\mu_{j}(A)u_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{k}^{A}u_{j}=P_{k}\circ R_{A}\circ P_{k}u_{j}=\mu_{j}(A)u_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k}u_{j}=u_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k}u_{j}=u_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{A})=\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(A)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{A})=\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(A)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we have for every j:</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(A)}-\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(B)}\leq\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{A})-\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(A)}-\frac{1}{\lambda_{j}(B)}\leq\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{A})-\mu_{j}(T_{k}^{B})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|T_{k}^{A}-T_{k}^{B}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|T_{k}^{A}-T_{k}^{B}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|P_{k}\circ R_{A}\circ P_{k}-P_{k}\circ R_{B}\circ P_{k}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|P_{k}\circ R_{A}\circ P_{k}-P_{k}\circ R_{B}\circ P_{k}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{|u|_{L^{2}}\leq 1}((P_{k}\circ R_{A}\circ P_{k}-P_{k}\circ R_{B}\circ P_{k})u,u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{|u|_{L^{2}}\leq 1}((P_{k}\circ R_{A}\circ P_{k}-P_{k}\circ R_{B}\circ P_{k})u,u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{|u|_{L^{2}}\leq 1}((R_{A}-R_{B})P_{k}u,P_{k}u)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{|u|_{L^{2}}\leq 1}((R_{A}-R_{B})P_{k}u,P_{k}u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="Sx2.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th eigenfunction, we note that:</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P_{k}u|_{L^{\infty}}=\sum_{i=1}^{k}a_{i}u_{i}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{k}|a_{i}||u_{i}|_{L^{\infty}}\leq C_{k}(A)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P_{k}u|_{L^{\infty}}=\sum_{i=1}^{k}a_{i}u_{i}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{k}|a_{i}||u_{i}|_{L^{\infty}}\leq C_{k}(A),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p3.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p3.9.1" class="ltx_text">by Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmthm12" title="Proposition 2.12. ‣ 2. Preliminaries ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.12</span></a>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
