<div id="Sx2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">proof of theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm19" title="Theorem 3.19. ‣ 3. Boundedness of Shape Minimizers ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.19</span></a></span>.
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Sx2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the previous lemma. there exists a constant <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> depending on <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}(A)}-\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}(B)}\right|\leq c_{k}(A)d_{\gamma}(A,B)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}(A)}-\frac{1}{\lambda_{k}(B)}\right|\leq c_{k}(A)d_{\gamma}(A,B).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(B)-E(A)\leq\frac{1}{2}d_{\gamma}(A,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(B)-E(A)\leq\frac{1}{2}d_{\gamma}(A,B)</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> small enough, such that <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\leq\frac{4c_{k}(A)}{\lambda_{k}(A)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\leq\frac{4c_{k}(A)}{\lambda_{k}(A)}</annotation></semantics></math> and for every <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\subset A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\subset A</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\gamma}(A,B)\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\gamma}(A,B)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}(B)-\lambda_{k}(A)\geq c^{\prime}_{k}(A)(E(B)-E(A))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}(B)-\lambda_{k}(A)\geq c^{\prime}_{k}(A)(E(B)-E(A))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">for a different constant <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> depending on <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,k,A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,k,A</annotation></semantics></math>. By (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>), we have <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A|-|B|\leq\lambda_{k}(B)-\lambda_{k}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A|-|B|\leq\lambda_{k}(B)-\lambda_{k}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, combining this and the above gives
<math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is a shape subsolution with <math id="Sx2.SS1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma=\frac{1}{c^{\prime}_{k}(A)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma=\frac{1}{c^{\prime}_{k}(A)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
