<section id="Sx2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">10.2. </span>Proof of theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm19" title="Theorem 5.19. ‣ 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.19</span></a></h3>

<div id="Sx2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="Sx2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a free boundary point. Let <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>-harmonic lifting of <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> in a ball <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> (similarly defined as in (<a href="#S5.E1" title="In 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>)). Let <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{h}</annotation></semantics></math> be its extension. Let <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> the the extension of <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, then for <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&lt;r&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&lt;r&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{B_{\rho}(x_{0},0)}|y|^{a}|\nabla{u}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{B_{\rho}(x_{0},0)}|y|^{a}|\nabla{u}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\int_{B_{\rho}}|y|^{a}|\nabla({u}-\tilde{h})|^{2}+2\int_{B_{\rho}}|y|^{a}|\nabla\tilde{h}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\int_{B_{\rho}}|y|^{a}|\nabla({u}-\tilde{h})|^{2}+2\int_{B_{\rho}}|y|^{a}|\nabla\tilde{h}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.27)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{((u_{\alpha}-h)(x)-(u_{\alpha}-h)(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}+2\left(\frac{\rho}{r}\right)^{n+1-|a|}\int_{B_{r}}|y|^{a}|\nabla\tilde{h}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}\frac{((u_{\alpha}-h)(x)-(u_{\alpha}-h)(y))^{2}}{|x-y|^{n+2s}}+2\left(\frac{\rho}{r}\right)^{n+1-|a|}\int_{B_{r}}|y|^{a}|\nabla\tilde{h}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.28)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq Cr^{n}+C\left(\frac{\rho}{r}\right)^{n+1-|a|}\int_{B_{r}}|y|^{a}|\nabla\tilde{h}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq Cr^{n}+C\left(\frac{\rho}{r}\right)^{n+1-|a|}\int_{B_{r}}|y|^{a}|\nabla\tilde{h}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq Cr^{n}+C\left(\frac{\rho}{r}\right)^{n+1-|a|}\int_{B_{r}}|y|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq Cr^{n}+C\left(\frac{\rho}{r}\right)^{n+1-|a|}\int_{B_{r}}|y|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm4" title="Proposition 5.4. ‣ 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm17" title="Lemma 5.17. ‣ 5. Optimal Regularity ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.17</span></a>. Now choose <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&lt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&lt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\delta^{k},\quad\rho=\delta^{k+1},\quad\mu=\delta^{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\delta^{k},\quad\rho=\delta^{k+1},\quad\mu=\delta^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{B_{\delta^{k+1}}}|y|^{a}|\nabla{u}|^{2}\leq C\mu^{k}+C\mu\delta^{1-|a|}\int_{B_{\delta^{k}}}|y|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></msub></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{B_{\delta^{k+1}}}|y|^{a}|\nabla{u}|^{2}\leq C\mu^{k}+C\mu\delta^{1-|a|}\int_{B_{\delta^{k}}}|y|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Now choose <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\delta^{1-|a|}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\delta^{1-|a|}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. By induction, we have</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{B_{\delta^{k}}}|x_{n}|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}\leq\frac{C^{2}}{1-C\delta^{1-|a|}}\mu^{k-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></msub></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{B_{\delta^{k}}}|x_{n}|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}\leq\frac{C^{2}}{1-C\delta^{1-|a|}}\mu^{k-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Then for all <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, and a different constant,</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.29)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{B_{r}(x^{\prime},0)}|x_{n}|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}\leq Cr^{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{B_{r}(x^{\prime},0)}|x_{n}|^{a}|\nabla u|^{2}\leq Cr^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">and we can conclude that</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{B_{r}(x^{\prime},0)}|\nabla u|\leq Cr^{n+s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{B_{r}(x^{\prime},0)}|\nabla u|\leq Cr^{n+s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">Now we can use Morrey’s theorem to conclude that</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.30)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|u(x^{\prime},0)-\overline{u_{B}}|\leq Cr^{s}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|u(x^{\prime},0)-\overline{u_{B}}|\leq Cr^{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">so that <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0,s}</annotation></semantics></math> in the thin space <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}\times\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{k}^{n}\times\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is left to show that we have the same Hölder growth in the <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x_{n}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x_{n}|</annotation></semantics></math> direction. For a fixed point <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y^{\prime},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y^{\prime},0)</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10.31)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}(x)=\frac{u((y^{\prime},0)+xr)-u(y^{\prime},0))}{r^{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}(x)=\frac{u((y^{\prime},0)+xr)-u(y^{\prime},0))}{r^{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#Sx2.E29" title="In Proof. ‣ 10.2. Proof of theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.29</span></a>), we have a universal <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> gradient bound in <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}=B_{1/2}(0,\cdots,0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}=B_{1/2}(0,\cdots,0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Using (<a href="#Sx2.E30" title="In Proof. ‣ 10.2. Proof of theorem ‣ Appendix ‣ Minimizing Eigenvalues of the Fractional Laplacian" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.30</span></a>) for <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|u_{r}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|u_{r}|</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that the average of <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|u_{r}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|u_{r}|</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{3/2}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{3/2}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> is universally bounded. Thus, the average of <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|u_{r}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|u_{r}|</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is universally bounded. By Poincare inequality in <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u_{r}\|_{{W^{1,2}}(B_{1/2}(0,\cdots,0,1))}\leq C." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u_{r}\|_{{W^{1,2}}(B_{1/2}(0,\cdots,0,1))}\leq C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.10.1" class="ltx_text">By first variation, <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm div}(|x_{n+1}|\nabla|u_{r}|)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm div}(|x_{n+1}|\nabla|u_{r}|)=0</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x_{n+1}|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x_{n+1}|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Away from the thin space, we use regularity theory for uniformly elliptic equations and conclude that each <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous in <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and we have the weak Harnack inequality</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u_{r}\|_{W^{1,2}(B_{1/4}(0,\cdots,0,1))}\leq C." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u_{r}\|_{W^{1,2}(B_{1/4}(0,\cdots,0,1))}\leq C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.11.1" class="ltx_text">This shows Hölder growth off the thin space, that is,</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{|u(y^{\prime},0)-u(x)|}{|(y^{\prime},0)-x|^{s}}\leq C." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{|u(y^{\prime},0)-u(x)|}{|(y^{\prime},0)-x|^{s}}\leq C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.12.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|y_{n+1}|\leq|x-y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|y_{n+1}|\leq|x-y|</annotation></semantics></math>, we may use the above to bound</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{|u(x)-u(y)|}{|x-y|^{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{|u(x)-u(y)|}{|x-y|^{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SS2.p1.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.SS2.p1.13.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="Sx2.SS2.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|y_{n+1}|&gt;|x-y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|y_{n+1}|&gt;|x-y|</annotation></semantics></math>, we then rescale with</span></p>
<table id="Sx2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
